My staff sent me this picture — my op-ed in print, sitting on the coffee table in my office.

The message is simple: the AI race will be won by those who can power it. Right now, red tape is slowing America down. We need reliable, abundant energy to lead. 

@ENERGY @SecretaryWright @housescience, let’s unleash American innovation through comprehensive federal strategy and win the AI race!

Safety matters. So does WINNING.

@nvidia's OpenShell is tackling AI safety the way America does best: by engineering solutions, not slowing innovation with more mandates from Washington.

Let our innovators innovate. Let our companies compete. And let’s stay ahead of China. https://t.co/0QgsbR7XpG

@AbdulElSayed has it all wrong. This is exactly the kind of rhetoric that stifles American innovation, undermines our technological leadership, and hands China a competitive advantage.
 
Let's be clear: AI is not an existential threat. Responsible safeguards and rapid innovation are not mutually exclusive. We can protect Americans without putting the brakes on progress and surrendering our lead to our adversaries.

https://t.co/O78NshUWzr
